module System

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rv` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Represents the aggregate protocol for entity values.
### `EntityType` identifies heap-backed or identity-bearing values whose
### semantics are based on shared instance identity rather than plain structural
### copying. An entity has `==` like a record does: the builder gives it `Equatable` when every member
### variable has `==` (its `eq` compares them), while `===` asks whether two names reach the same entity.
@rv("EntityType")
protocol EntityType
